    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0183" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg163"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 680.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 15, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On the 7th instant I submitted to the
                    Secretary of Navy, for his concurrence, the draught of my despatch to you (No.
                    675) relative to the adoption of precautionary measures in regard to the two
                    clipper ships at St. Nazaire believed to be building for the insurgents.</p>
                <p>I now give you a copy of Mr. Welles’s reply of the 10th instant, together with a
                    copy of his instructions to Commodore Craven, of the Niagara, and Captain Walke,
                    of the Sacramento.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d216-a1.xml" xpointer="d216-a1"/>
            </div>
